# AgentOS model credentials.
#
# This file is read by the agentos-core service when it starts. It is NOT
# installed by any package: create it yourself, with the permissions the service
# requires.
#
#   sudo install -m 0600 -o root -g root /dev/null /etc/agentos/credentials.env
#   sudoedit /etc/agentos/credentials.env
#   sudo systemctl restart agentos-core
#
# The service refuses to read this file when it is readable by group or other,
# because a model credential must not be visible to any other account. The file
# is never printed by agentosctl, never written to the database, never placed in
# an event payload, and never copied into the audit trail: only the variable
# names are allowed through, and only names on a fixed allowlist.
#
# Do not put a credential in /etc/agentos/agentos.toml, in a systemd unit, or on
# a command line: those are readable by other users and are recorded in shell
# history.
#
# Recognised variables:
#   DEEPSEEK_API_KEY  the model credential itself
#   DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL optional alternative API base URL
#   HTTP_PROXY        optional egress proxy
#   HTTPS_PROXY       optional egress proxy
#   NO_PROXY          optional proxy bypass list
#
# Example (replace the value, then save):
#
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=replace-me
